  "observations": [
    "524878 reads B,G,R,A source bytes into native R,G,B,A destination and computes A*byte61c294/255. R5900 MULT5248ec explicitly encodes rd=v0 (standard MIPS decompiler omits that destination).",
    "Default61c28c/d retain indexed formats;61c294 initializes native alpha maximum128. Format14 table target525168 uses256-entry palette;format16 target525580 uses16-entry palette.",
    "Format16 indexed4 branch5257ec keeps packed bytes; alternate indexed8 branch5257b4..c4 explicitly writes low then high nibble.",
    "2b7498 format6 copies16 native RGBA palette words verbatim before upload; 8bitCSM1 upload swizzle is a permutation, not a logical color change."
  ],
  "claim_limits": [
    "Static decoding for original boot/default image-loader settings, not a runtime texture capture.",
    "This decoder reads logical texels; GS rasterization and image sampling belong to the separate native renderer."
  ]
